      "math_academy_id": "e-4704",
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $C$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14118900/assets/ed9acf39f48a8ffef212858a0d1c0ce572af4f2466c66f8b07fa2df313e2d953.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $C$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14118900/assets/33ca8efbcad5138b311b1cd3844f7138895098b4fa31fd26d04ed32f7e1f1d7c.svg)\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column.",
